<section data-screen-label="FAQ" id="faq" style="background:var(--paper);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Common questions</span>
<h2 style="margin:0 0 clamp(28px,3.4vw,40px);max-width:28ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">Frequently Asked Questions About Stem Cell Therapy for Knees</h2>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);max-width:960px">
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Does stem cell therapy work for knee osteoarthritis?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Some randomized studies suggest certain cell-based treatments may improve pain and function, while others find little or no advantage over placebo or conventional injections. The result depends heavily on the exact product, protocol and patient.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">What is the success rate of stem cell therapy for knees?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">There is no scientifically meaningful universal success rate. “Success” can refer to pain reduction, improved function, structural change or avoiding surgery, and rates vary by product, population and follow-up period.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Can stem cells regrow knee cartilage?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Routine intra-articular stem-cell injections have not been shown to reliably regenerate durable normal knee cartilage. Symptom improvement and cartilage regeneration should not be treated as the same outcome.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">How long does stem cell therapy for knees last?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">There is no established universal duration. Trials usually follow patients for months to one or two years, and durability varies by product and population. Long-term evidence is less mature than short-term symptom evidence.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Which type of stem cell is best for knees?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">No cell source, product or dose has been established as universally superior for knee osteoarthritis. Treatment comparisons should focus on the exact product, manufacturing, evidence and diagnosis.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Is BMAC the same as stem cell therapy?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Not exactly. BMAC is concentrated bone marrow containing many cell types and biological factors. It is different from a purified or culture-expanded MSC product.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Is PRP a stem-cell treatment?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">No. PRP is produced from concentrated platelets in blood. It belongs to the broader orthobiologics/regenerative-medicine category but is not a therapeutic stem-cell product.</p>
</details>
<details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-on-light)">
<summary style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 2px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Can stem cells prevent knee replacement?<span data-plus="true" style="flex:0 0 auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--sand-700);transition:transform var(--duration-standard) var(--ease-standard)">+</span></summary>
<p style="margin:0;padding:0 2px 24px;max-width:70ch;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Current evidence has not established that stem-cell injections reliably prevent future knee replacement. A clinician should evaluate whether non-surgical treatment remains medically reasonable for your specific knee.</p>
</details>
</div>
</div>
</section>
